<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The worker, hourly, on Katherine's Mac.

  A LaunchAGENT, not a LaunchDaemon, and that is load-bearing rather than a
  preference. get_credentials() shells out to `security find-generic-password`,
  which only answers inside a logged-in user session with the keychain
  unlocked. A daemon runs outside one and would fail every hour forever.

  INSTALL (it does not install itself):
      cp tools/schlage/com.rentaldirect.schlage-worker.plist \
         ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.rentaldirect.schlage-worker.plist
  STOP:
      launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.rentaldirect.schlage-worker.plist

  THE VENV PATH IS EXPLICIT. Plain python3 has no pyschlage, and a scheduled job
  has no shell profile, no PATH you have tuned, and no activated environment.

  IT ONLY RUNS WHILE THE MAC IS AWAKE, which is accepted: a code has to be on a
  door by 4pm check-in, so hours of slack are fine. A missed interval fires once
  on wake. What is NOT accepted is nobody noticing a long silence, and that is
  the heartbeat panel's job — last-drain age climbs whether the cause is a dead
  credential, a stale copy, or a lid that stayed shut.

  NO SECRETS HERE. The Schlage password is in the login keychain and the
  Supabase key is read from .env.local by the worker itself. Nothing in this
  file is sensitive, which is why it can live in the repo.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.rentaldirect.schlage-worker</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/katherine/Desktop/schlage-venv/bin/python</string>
        <string>/Users/katherine/Desktop/schlage-worker.py</string>
        <string>--commit</string>
    </array>

    <!-- schlage_creds.py sits beside the worker and is imported by name -->
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/katherine/Desktop</string>

    <!-- hourly. The backlog drains one code per door per run, so a deep queue
         clears over successive runs instead of manual repeats. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>3600</integer>

    <!-- catch up as soon as the Mac is back, rather than waiting out the hour -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- the traceback lands in a file instead of a terminal nobody has open -->
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/katherine/Library/Logs/schlage-worker.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/katherine/Library/Logs/schlage-worker.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
